{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, every command run through sudo is recorded in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with the invoking user and timestamp.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Sudo was configured to use the dedicated logfile, with valid sudoers syntax and unwrapped records. Direct tests before and after restart show timestamped records containing the invoking user, target user, working directory, and complete command. The configuration and earlier records persisted across the restart, and fresh logging succeeded afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-05594ad5d81c4aa4","cmd-3f7dfdd4f73a4541","cmd-d46aecdcfde64d8a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Sudo command entries are kept out of the general system logs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The configuration disables sudo command syslog output. Unique command markers written to the dedicated log were directly shown absent from /var/log/messages, /var/log/secure, and journald both before and after restart. Journal PAM session events may remain, but the tested sudo command entries and markers did not.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f00e700a99424ca2","cmd-3f7dfdd4f73a4541","cmd-d46aecdcfde64d8a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were unchanged before and after the work and restart. The implementation uses the installed sudo and logrotate facilities; the command trace contains no software installation or OS/kernel replacement, and final package health remained normal.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d63bbe316a5a4cc9","cmd-0259d05fed5c4b80","cmd-3f7dfdd4f73a4541","cmd-d46aecdcfde64d8a","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"The complete command timeline shows no unnecessary mutation. Persistent changes—the sudoers fragment, protected logfile, and rotation policy—directly support the requested outcome. Marker-generating sudo commands were bounded verification, and the scheduled reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. The first configuration attempt created only temporary draft files; validation rejected the unsupported logfile_mode setting before installation, and the trap removed the drafts, so it left no persistent mutation and directly informed the corrected implementation. Subsequent replacement of the fragment corrected line wrapping and fail-open behavior. Lifecycle snapshots show no failed services, new listeners, package damage, or abandoned temporary files attributable to the executor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ccb4c52dc7794fc1","cmd-7870a6c68a734f93","cmd-05594ad5d81c4aa4","cmd-915427af6259460b","cmd-d46aecdcfde64d8a","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Native sudo logging writes timestamped, user-attributed command records to the requested protected file while tested command entries remain absent from general logs. The behavior, configuration, and existing data survived a full node restart, and the original RHEL release and kernel were preserved. The mandatory restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged scheduling and observed disconnect, changed boot identity, recovered services/system state, persisted data, and successful fresh logging; fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The universal claim that every possible sudo invocation is logged is supported by the effective global sudo configuration and representative pre-/post-restart probes, but captured evidence cannot exercise every user, command form, or failure path.","No package transaction-history query was captured; preservation is instead supported by the complete command trace, unchanged platform observations, use of already-installed components, and healthy final package state."]}
